WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.988
Every audience sees, hears and processes information differently.

2
00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:10.063
A few simple fixes make your slides work for every viewer, and clearer for everyone.

3
00:00:10.563 --> 00:00:14.902
Low contrast is the most common problem, and one of the easiest to fix.

4
00:00:14.952 --> 00:00:19.849
Aim for four and a half to one for normal text, and three to one for large text.

5
00:00:20.963 --> 00:00:28.217
Use near-black text on light backgrounds, put a solid panel behind text on photos, and always test with a checker.

6
00:00:29.363 --> 00:00:31.914
Some viewers can't tell red from green.

7
00:00:31.964 --> 00:00:37.349
Give each status a label and an icon, and let colour be an extra cue, not the only one.

8
00:00:38.599 --> 00:00:43.588
Big, plain, left-aligned text reads well in a room and on a small screen.

9
00:00:43.638 --> 00:00:48.664
Body text at 24 point or larger, headlines at 36 or larger.

10
00:00:49.164 --> 00:00:57.034
When a deck becomes a video, turn on captions, and let the voice explain what a chart shows, not just say 'as you can see here'.

11
00:00:58.284 --> 00:01:00.928
Accessible slides make better videos.

12
00:01:00.978 --> 00:01:05.688
On Pro, AI directs the video, timing animation to your narration.

13
00:01:05.738 --> 00:01:09.149
Try Basic first at powerpoint2vid.com.

